{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "brislane-lending-platform-v2",
    "name": "Brislane Lending Platform API",
    "description": "Phase 3 — API Quality Engineering & Security.\n\n## SETUP (do this first)\n1. Go to your Postman workspace\n2. Click 'Mock Servers' in the left sidebar\n3. Click '+ Create Mock Server'\n4. Select 'Create a new collection' → name it anything\n5. Copy the Mock Server URL (looks like https://xxxxxxxx.mock.pstmn.io)\n6. Click this collection → Variables tab → paste it as the value for 'base_url'\n\n## THEN RUN IN ORDER\nRun request 1 (POST Login) first — it saves your token automatically.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "PASTE_YOUR_MOCK_SERVER_URL_HERE",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Your Postman Mock Server URL — e.g. https://xxxxxxxx.mock.pstmn.io"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-set by POST Login request. Do not edit manually."
    },
    {
      "key": "application_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Auto-set by POST Loan Application request."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🔐 1. POST Login (run first)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Response has token', function() {",
              "    var json = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(json.token).to.be.a('string');",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', json.token);",
              "    console.log('✅ Token saved to collection variable');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Token type is Bearer', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().token_type).to.eql('Bearer');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"test.candidate@brislane.com\",\n  \"password\": \"TestPass123!\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        },
        "description": "⚠️ TECH DEBT FIX APPLIED HERE\n\nThe original inherited collection had a hardcoded expired bearer token on every request — all calls 401'd immediately.\n\nFix: Added this login request. The test script saves the returned JWT to {{access_token}}, which all subsequent requests use via 'Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}'.\n\nThis is the correct Postman pattern for dynamic auth."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "👥 2. GET Customers",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Response is an array', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Each customer has id, email, first_name', function() {",
              "    var customers = pm.response.json();",
              "    customers.forEach(function(c) {",
              "        pm.expect(c).to.have.property('id');",
              "        pm.expect(c).to.have.property('email');",
              "        pm.expect(c).to.have.property('first_name');",
              "    });",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"}],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["customers"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "📋 3. POST Loan Application",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 201 Created', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Response has application id', function() {",
              "    var json = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(json.id).to.be.a('string');",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('application_id', json.id);",
              "    console.log('✅ Application ID saved:', json.id);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Status is draft', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('draft');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"},
          {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"customer_id\": \"C1000001\",\n  \"loan_amount\": 5000,\n  \"loan_term_months\": 24,\n  \"purpose\": \"home_improvement\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/loans/applications",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["loans", "applications"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "✅ 4. PUT Loan Submit",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Status is submitted', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('submitted');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Response has reference number', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().reference).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"},
          {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"application_id\": \"{{application_id}}\",\n  \"declaration_accepted\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/loans/submit",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["loans", "submit"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "💳 5. GET Payments",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200 OK', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Response is an array', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Each payment has id, amount, due_date', function() {",
              "    var payments = pm.response.json();",
              "    payments.forEach(function(p) {",
              "        pm.expect(p).to.have.property('id');",
              "        pm.expect(p).to.have.property('amount');",
              "        pm.expect(p).to.have.property('due_date');",
              "    });",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"}],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/payments",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["payments"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "🔒 SEC-1: Expired JWT → expect 401",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Expired token returns 401 Unauthorized', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('Error references token/auth', function() {",
              "    var body = pm.response.text().toLowerCase();",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.satisfy(function(b) {",
              "        return b.includes('token') || b.includes('unauthorized') || b.includes('expired') || b.includes('invalid');",
              "    });",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJDMTAwMDAwMSIsImlhdCI6MTcwMDAwMDAwMCwiZXhwIjoxNzAwMDAwMDAxfQ.EXPIRED_FOR_TESTING"}],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["customers"]
        },
        "description": "PSD2/SCA Test: Send a JWT with exp claim in the past.\nExpected: 401 Unauthorized\nVerifies: Server validates token expiry, not just presence."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "🔒 SEC-2: Tampered JWT → expect 401",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Tampered token returns 401 Unauthorized', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJDMTAwMDAwMSIsInJvbGUiOiJhZG1pbiJ9.TAMPERED_SIGNATURE_XXXXX"}],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["customers"]
        },
        "description": "Security Test: Modify the JWT signature.\nExpected: 401 Unauthorized\nVerifies: Server validates full token integrity, not just payload."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "🔒 SEC-3: No token → expect 401",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Missing token returns 401 Unauthorized', function() {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/loans/applications",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["loans", "applications"]
        },
        "description": "Security Test: No Authorization header at all.\nExpected: 401 Unauthorized\nVerifies: Unauthenticated requests are always rejected."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "🔒 SEC-4: Rate Limit → expect 429",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Response is 429 (rate limited) or 200 (under limit)', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 429]);",
              "});",
              "if (pm.response.code === 429) {",
              "    console.log('✅ Rate limit confirmed — 429 received');",
              "} else {",
              "    console.log('Under rate limit threshold — run via Collection Runner 15+ times to trigger 429');",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [
          {"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"},
          {"key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json"}
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"application_id\": \"rate-limit-test\",\n  \"declaration_accepted\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/loans/submit",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["loans", "submit"]
        },
        "description": "Rate Limit Test: Run via Collection Runner 15+ times rapidly.\nExpected: Eventually returns 429 Too Many Requests\nVerifies: /loans/submit enforces rate limiting per FCA requirement."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "🔒 SEC-5: Cross-customer access → expect 403",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Cross-customer access blocked (401 or 403)', function() {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([401, 403]);",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{"key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"}],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/customers/C1999999/loans",
          "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
          "path": ["customers", "C1999999", "loans"]
        },
        "description": "Role-Based Access Test: Use own token to access a different customer's data.\nExpected: 403 Forbidden (or 401)\nVerifies: Role-based access controls prevent cross-customer data access.\nFCA Consumer Duty requirement."
      }
    }
  ]
}
